    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n851" root="اصد" body-key="A">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أصّدهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأْصِيدٌ</span>, is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُصْدَةٌ</span>: (S, K:)
[app. meaning <i>He made it an</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُصْدَة</span>: or <i>he wore
it as an</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُصْدَة</span>: and hence <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤَصَّدٌ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤَصَّدَةٌ</span> as
explained below: or] <i>he clad him with an</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُصْدَة</span>.
(TK.)

